        text: 'You cannot use the Hague return process, and your home-country custody order is not directly enforceable in the UAE. Your options are: (1) contact your own government (in the UK the FCDO, in the US the State Department’s Office of Children’s Issues) and, in the UK, the charity Reunite; they can advise and raise the case with UAE authorities but cannot force a return; (2) instruct a UAE family lawyer and start custody proceedings in the UAE court, where your foreign order can be submitted as evidence and the court decides on the child’s best interests; (3) ask a lawyer in your home country about criminal and other remedies there. Act immediately, because delay makes a return less likely.',
