        text: 'Ask the UAE court for a travel ban on the child, as part of a custody case or as an urgent standalone application. Once a ban is registered, the child is stopped at UAE ports of departure. The law also helps: under Article 116 of Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2024 a custodial parent needs the other parent’s written consent, or the court’s permission, to travel abroad with the child, and under Article 117 the guardian (normally the father) usually keeps the child’s passport except when the child travels. If your case runs under a different law, such as the civil personal status law for non-Muslims, ask the court to write travel conditions into the order. Act before there is a flight booking, not after.',
