      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How does the UAE airport travel ban for children work?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'A court travel ban is registered with the UAE immigration and border authorities. When the child’s documents are presented at a UAE airport, land border or seaport, the ban shows up and the child is stopped from leaving. The ban should list every passport the child holds, because a ban logged against one document number may not catch another. It is a preventive tool: it stops a departure, it cannot bring back a child who has already left.',
